<title>BELGIUM: Belgian money market supply raised in week.</title>
<headline>Belgian money market supply raised in week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian National Bank said it added liquidity to the money market in the week ended Monday to offset a rise in notes in circulation.</p>
<p>(figures from the  weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves	   409.738 ( - 0.031)</p>
<p> Advances against pledged security   9.917 ( - 2.507)</p>
<p> Commercial bills			  3.367 ( + 0.048)</p>
<p> Securities portfolio		   23.317 ( + 0.001)</p>
<p> Money market interventions	  109.283 ( + 3.456)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   447.823 ( + 3.297)</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710 $ $</p>
